<title>USA: FOCUS-Toys R Us gives Baby needed growth formula.</title>
<headline>FOCUS-Toys R Us gives Baby needed growth formula.</headline>
<byline>Jennifer Westhoven</byline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Baby Superstore Inc's merger into Toys R Us Inc marks a new growth phase for the company, which exploded onto the stock market in 1994 but has been suffering sharp growing pains in the past few months.</p>
<p>The retailer will be bought by Toys R Us for $376 million in a deal that gives holders about $23.45 for each of their share, but gives founder Jack Tate only about $15 for each of his shares.</p>
</text>
